1
00:00:04,250 --> 00:00:06,040
Oh, come on!

2
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:08,750
Hey, it's your Thanksgiving too.

3
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:11,300
You know, instead of watching football, you could help.

4
00:00:11,460 --> 00:00:13,170
We know.

5
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:17,970
Rachel, you wanna put the marshmallows in concentric circles.

6
00:00:19,430 --> 00:00:22,430
No, you want to put them in concentric circles.

7
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:24,640
I want to do this.

8
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:36,070
Every year.

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,500
# So no one told you life was gonna be this way #

10
00:00:47,070 --> 00:00:51,240
# Your job's a joke, you're broke, your love life's D.O.A. #

11
00:00:52,150 --> 00:00:55,960
# It's like you're always stuck in second gear #

12
00:00:56,420 --> 00:00:58,520
# When it hasn't been your day, #

13
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:01,520
# your week, your month, or even your year #

14
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:05,480
# but I'll be there for you #

15
00:01:05,480 --> 00:01:07,310
# When the rain starts to pour #

16
00:01:07,310 --> 00:01:10,430
# I'll be there for you #

17
00:01:10,430 --> 00:01:12,270
# Like I've been there before #

18
00:01:12,270 --> 00:01:15,280
# I'll be there for you #

19
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:18,940
# 'Cause you're there for me too #

20
00:01:23,410 --> 00:01:25,700
To the 10, to the 5. Touchdown, Giants!

21
00:01:26,540 --> 00:01:31,170
You know, for once, I am gonna try to watch one of these things.

22
00:01:32,340 --> 00:01:33,750
Halftime.

23
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:38,930
Who wants to, uh, throw the ball around? Get a little 3-on-3 going?

24
00:01:39,090 --> 00:01:41,800
- Oh, that would be so much fun!     - Can I play too?

25
00:01:41,970 --> 00:01:44,390
I've never played football, ever.

26
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:46,020
Great! You can cover Chandler.

27
00:01:48,730 --> 00:01:50,400
I don't... I don't really want to play.

28
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:53,610
You never do anything since you and Janice broke up.

29
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:54,820
Not true.

30
00:01:54,980 --> 00:01:58,530
I wanted to wear my bathrobe and eat peanut clusters all day.

31
00:01:58,700 --> 00:02:01,990
And start drinking in the morning. Don't say I don't have goals!

32
00:02:02,830 --> 00:02:05,370
You have to start getting over her, all right?

33
00:02:05,540 --> 00:02:09,330
If you play, maybe it'll take your mind off Janice.

34
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:13,960
If you don't, everyone will be mad at you because the teams won't be even.

35
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:15,960
All right, I'll play.

36
00:02:16,130 --> 00:02:18,380
Yay! Let's do it! Ross?

37
00:02:18,550 --> 00:02:20,510
- What?     - Wanna play football?

38
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:26,680
Monica and I aren't supposed to play football.

39
00:02:27,310 --> 00:02:29,890
Says who? Your mom? Ha-ha-ha.

40
00:02:30,310 --> 00:02:31,350
Yes.

41
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:37,900
Ahem. Every Thanksgiving, um, we used to have a touch football game...

42
00:02:38,070 --> 00:02:39,700
...called The Geller Bowl.

43
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:42,200
No, no, no. You say that proudly!

44
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:46,700
Anyway, Ross and I were always captains, and, um...

45
00:02:46,870 --> 00:02:50,540
It got kind of competitive. And one year, Geller Bowl VI...

46
00:02:50,710 --> 00:02:53,960
...I accidentally broke Ross' nose.

47
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:57,590
It was so not an accident.

48
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:59,840
She saw I was about to tag her, so she threw...

49
00:03:00,010 --> 00:03:03,140
...her big fat grandma-arm elbow in my face...

50
00:03:03,300 --> 00:03:05,220
...and just kept running.

51
00:03:05,390 --> 00:03:07,390
To score the winning touchdown, by the way.

52
00:03:09,350 --> 00:03:12,230
Uh, you did not win the game. The touchdown didn't count...

53
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:17,320
...because of the spectacularly illegal, and savage, nose-breaking.

54
00:03:18,570 --> 00:03:19,860
I won the game.

55
00:03:20,030 --> 00:03:23,450
Yeah? Then how come you didn't get the Geller Cup?

56
00:03:24,620 --> 00:03:26,910
Ahem, there was a Geller Cup?

57
00:03:27,580 --> 00:03:30,250
Yes, the trophy you got if you won the game.

58
00:03:30,410 --> 00:03:33,830
But Dad said nobody won, and he was sick of our fighting.

59
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,250
So he took the trophy...

60
00:03:42,550 --> 00:03:44,510
...threw it in the lake.

61
00:03:45,260 --> 00:03:47,260
And was the curse lifted?

62
00:03:49,350 --> 00:03:50,970
Anyway...

63
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:54,440
...Mom said we weren't allowed to play football again.

64
00:03:55,060 --> 00:03:57,980
You know what? I think we should play a game.

65
00:03:58,150 --> 00:04:00,030
I mean, come on. It's been 12 years.

66
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:02,950
Can I see you for a second?

67
00:04:07,410 --> 00:04:08,450
Wuss!

68
00:04:08,620 --> 00:04:10,990
All right, we're gonna play.

69
00:04:11,450 --> 00:04:15,330
Wait. How we gonna get there? My mom won't let me cross the street.

70
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:22,300
Here you go.

71
00:04:22,670 --> 00:04:23,720
All right.

72
00:04:23,880 --> 00:04:25,510
- Let's bring it in.     - Wait.

73
00:04:25,680 --> 00:04:27,140
Honey, throw it to me!

74
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:29,550
Here you go.

75
00:04:31,100 --> 00:04:33,770
That almost hit me in the face!

76
00:04:33,940 --> 00:04:35,730
We have to pick captains.

77
00:04:35,900 --> 00:04:38,150
And then "Tennilles."

78
00:04:40,190 --> 00:04:41,650
So how do we decide that?

79
00:04:41,820 --> 00:04:44,070
- Why don't we just bunny up?     - What?

80
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:46,320
- Bunny!     - Bunny!

81
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:49,160
Looks like Ross and I are captains.

82
00:04:49,330 --> 00:04:53,200
Okay, so, um, I bunnied first, so I get to pick first. Joey.

83
00:04:53,370 --> 00:04:55,330
- Thank you.     - Monica.

84
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:57,330
I'm your best friend.

85
00:04:57,500 --> 00:04:59,710
Sweetie, don't worry, you'll get picked.

86
00:04:59,880 --> 00:05:01,710
Chandler.

87
00:05:03,840 --> 00:05:05,630
- Ross?     - Phoebe.

88
00:05:09,300 --> 00:05:10,970
Sweetie, now I pick you.

89
00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:14,560
You don't pick me. You're stuck with me!

90
00:05:15,390 --> 00:05:16,890
Okay. All right. So let's see.

91
00:05:17,060 --> 00:05:20,310
Let's play from the, uh, trash can to the light post, right?

92
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:21,860
Two-hand touch. We'll kick off.

93
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:24,740
People, listen. I've got 28 minutes...

94
00:05:24,900 --> 00:05:27,070
...before I have to baste again.

95
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:29,200
Wow, just like in the pros.

96
00:05:29,370 --> 00:05:31,530
Okay, huddle up! Whoo!

97
00:05:31,700 --> 00:05:35,410
- Huddle up over here!     - Wait for me! Wait for me!

98
00:05:35,710 --> 00:05:37,500
Oh, cool! My first huddle.

99
00:05:37,670 --> 00:05:39,500
- Okay.     - Ha, ha. Okay.

100
00:05:39,670 --> 00:05:42,790
So what do you guys really think of Chandler?

101
00:05:44,380 --> 00:05:47,090
- You know what you're doing, right?     - Yeah.

102
00:05:47,260 --> 00:05:49,550
Okay. Joey will catch it. We'll block.

103
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:51,390
What's "block"?

104
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:55,680
- I thought you knew what you were doing.     - I thought you meant in life!

105
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:58,230
Break!

106
00:05:58,390 --> 00:06:01,610
The ball is Janice. The ball is Janice.

107
00:06:06,940 --> 00:06:09,200
Ow! Son of a...! Ow!

108
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:11,410
- Come on!     - I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

109
00:06:11,570 --> 00:06:14,080
You know what? We're just gonna throw it.

110
00:06:15,660 --> 00:06:16,910
I got it!

111
00:06:17,080 --> 00:06:18,500
Go, go, go!

112
00:06:27,300 --> 00:06:30,470
Score! Seven to nothing!

113
00:06:30,970 --> 00:06:31,970
Honey, you okay?

114
00:06:32,140 --> 00:06:33,470
Come on, let's go.

115
00:06:33,640 --> 00:06:35,310
Whoo. Losers walk.

116
00:06:35,470 --> 00:06:38,140
Yeah? Losers talk.

117
00:06:38,310 --> 00:06:40,940
No, no, actually, losers rhyme.

118
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:44,360
43
Forty-three...

119
00:06:44,520 --> 00:06:45,610
74
...Seventy-four...

120
00:06:49,780 --> 00:06:51,280
- You wanna go shotgun?     - Yeah.

121
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:54,870
Hike.

122
00:06:55,030 --> 00:06:57,950
- One Mississippi...     - Over here! Over here! Unh.

123
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:00,040
Ha! I almost caught that one!

124
00:07:01,620 --> 00:07:04,630
Great. Now the score's seven to almost seven.

125
00:07:05,170 --> 00:07:09,800
Okay, on this play, I want you to do a down-and-out to the right, okay?

126
00:07:09,970 --> 00:07:11,760
- Break!     - Wait. What am I gonna do?

127
00:07:11,930 --> 00:07:13,220
You?

128
00:07:13,390 --> 00:07:14,430
You go long.

129
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:15,890
How long?

130
00:07:16,060 --> 00:07:17,890
Until we start to look very small.

131
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:20,770
- Okay. Break!     - Break!

132
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:22,980
- Set, hike!     - One Mississippi...

133
00:07:23,150 --> 00:07:24,860
Switch! Switch! Switch!

134
00:07:25,020 --> 00:07:26,770
No, no, no, no!

135
00:07:35,950 --> 00:07:38,160
Hey. Thanks for stopping our ball.

136
00:07:38,330 --> 00:07:40,290
You are playing American football?

137
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:41,500
Yeah.

138
00:07:41,660 --> 00:07:44,710
Wow, you're, like, from a whole other country!

139
00:07:45,420 --> 00:07:48,550
- I'm Dutch.     - Hi, I'm Joey.

140
00:07:49,010 --> 00:07:50,260
I am Margha.

141
00:07:51,050 --> 00:07:54,050
Sorry, Dutch, I didn't get that last little bit.

142
00:07:54,220 --> 00:07:56,890
You wanna play football or...? Hi, I'm Chandler.

143
00:07:57,050 --> 00:07:58,930
Hello, Chandler.

144
00:07:59,100 --> 00:08:02,520
Her name is Dutch and also "Margham."

145
00:08:03,230 --> 00:08:05,270
- Margha.     - Margha.

146
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:06,560
Margha.

147
00:08:06,730 --> 00:08:09,440
Mahan.

148
00:08:10,190 --> 00:08:12,780
Come on, guys! Let's go! Second down!

149
00:08:13,740 --> 00:08:16,780
- Uh, hello? It's third down.     - No, it's not. It's second.

150
00:08:17,950 --> 00:08:19,990
"Wow" what?

151
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:24,080
It just amazes me that you're still pulling stuff like this. Heh.

152
00:08:24,750 --> 00:08:28,710
- Pulling what? It's second down.     - Okay, it's second down.

153
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:31,630
Take all the second downs you need.

154
00:08:31,880 --> 00:08:34,550
- I heard that.     - Well, I said it loud.

155
00:08:36,430 --> 00:08:38,550
It is okay if I stay and watch?

156
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:41,890
- Just sit right there.     - Yeah, why don't you stick around?

157
00:08:42,060 --> 00:08:43,770
- That went well.     - I think so.

158
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:46,900
I was thinking about, uh, asking her for her number.

159
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:50,940
Thanks, man, but it makes a stronger statement if I ask for it myself.

160
00:08:53,150 --> 00:08:57,910
I was thinking about for me, as part of that getting-over-Janice thing.

161
00:08:58,530 --> 00:09:00,120
Oh, yeah. That.

162
00:09:00,950 --> 00:09:02,870
If it means that much, I'll let you have her.

163
00:09:03,040 --> 00:09:04,120
Thanks.

164
00:09:05,040 --> 00:09:07,120
Wh...? "Let me have her"?

165
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:10,590
You mean if you didn't, I wouldn't have a shot?

166
00:09:11,210 --> 00:09:13,590
I don't like to say it out loud...

167
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:15,380
...but yeah!

168
00:09:16,760 --> 00:09:20,140
We all have our strengths. You're better with numbers and stuff.

169
00:09:20,890 --> 00:09:23,890
Math? You're giving me math?

170
00:09:24,810 --> 00:09:27,140
All right, you know what? Forget about it.

171
00:09:27,310 --> 00:09:29,690
You go for the girl. We'll see who gets her.

172
00:09:33,820 --> 00:09:37,030
I want you to run a post-pattern to the left. And, sweetie...

173
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:38,530
Yeah, I know. Go long.

174
00:09:38,700 --> 00:09:41,280
All I'm doing is running back and forth from the huddle.

175
00:09:42,910 --> 00:09:46,580
Well, uh, you wanna just stay out there?

176
00:09:47,160 --> 00:09:49,250
- Can I see that for a second?     - Yeah.

177
00:09:52,170 --> 00:09:54,460
- Okay.     - Okay, let's go.

178
00:09:54,630 --> 00:09:56,170
- I got Chandler     - Hike!

179
00:09:56,340 --> 00:09:58,970
One Mississippi, two Mississippi, three Mississippi.

180
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:00,680
Fumble!

181
00:10:06,930 --> 00:10:09,640
What's the matter with you? This is my favorite jersey.

182
00:10:10,190 --> 00:10:12,270
Well, now you have two.

183
00:10:13,770 --> 00:10:15,650
Hey, I am good at math!

184
00:10:16,610 --> 00:10:18,860
That's it. I was still gonna let you have her.

185
00:10:19,030 --> 00:10:21,780
But now, prepare to feel bad about yourself.

186
00:10:21,950 --> 00:10:25,290
I've been preparing for that my entire life!

187
00:10:25,950 --> 00:10:28,160
Or something about you that's mean!

188
00:10:28,710 --> 00:10:30,500
Come on, guys. Let's go.

189
00:10:30,710 --> 00:10:32,580
Tie score. We're running out of time.

190
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:34,250
Forty-two, 38, hike!

191
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:37,670
I got it! Ooh! Ugh!

192
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:40,130
Broken boobs! Ow.

193
00:10:40,300 --> 00:10:42,720
- Pheebs, run!     - Run, Phoebe! Run!

194
00:10:42,890 --> 00:10:45,930
- God! Touchdown! Touchdown!     - Yes! Touchdown! Hey, oh!

195
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:49,020
No, no, no.

196
00:10:49,190 --> 00:10:51,850
Uh, the buzzer buzzed. It doesn't count.

197
00:10:52,190 --> 00:10:54,110
- After the snap.     - Before the snap.

198
00:10:54,270 --> 00:10:55,480
- After.     - Before.

199
00:10:55,690 --> 00:10:57,400
- Does it really matter?     - Yes!

200
00:10:57,650 --> 00:11:01,280
But I made a touchdown. It was my first touchdown.

201
00:11:01,450 --> 00:11:04,240
Pheebs, that's great. Doesn't count.

202
00:11:04,410 --> 00:11:07,040
- Does so count.     - Cheater, cheater, compulsive eater.

203
00:11:08,830 --> 00:11:10,710
Oh, my God!

204
00:11:11,830 --> 00:11:15,670
That's fine. Maybe you haven't grown up, but I have.

205
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:17,590
- Oh, okay.     - Dead leg!

206
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:23,260
Okay, fine. You want to win by cheating, go ahead.

207
00:11:23,430 --> 00:11:25,390
The touchdown does count. You win.

208
00:11:25,550 --> 00:11:27,680
No!

209
00:11:28,770 --> 00:11:32,640
I won't do this again. I wanna beat you when you can't blame it...

210
00:11:32,810 --> 00:11:36,730
...on the broken nose or the buzzer or the fact that you might have mono.

211
00:11:36,900 --> 00:11:40,360
Let's just call this tie score and it's halftime.

212
00:11:40,530 --> 00:11:42,110
First, I don't play with cheaters.

213
00:11:42,280 --> 00:11:45,280
Second of all, you know I had swollen glands!

214
00:11:47,450 --> 00:11:49,580
You know what? I think you'll play.

215
00:11:50,290 --> 00:11:52,000
Oh, really? Why's that?

216
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:54,040
Because the winner gets this.

217
00:11:54,670 --> 00:11:56,840
The Geller Cup!

218
00:11:59,340 --> 00:12:02,340
Is everybody else seeing a troll doll nailed to a two-by-four?

219
00:12:03,930 --> 00:12:06,050
Okay, good.

220
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:13,520
Okay, where the hell did you get that?

221
00:12:13,690 --> 00:12:15,980
When you went to the hospital for your nose...

222
00:12:16,150 --> 00:12:18,980
...I swam into the lake and fished it out.

223
00:12:19,150 --> 00:12:20,280
That cup is mine!

224
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:23,570
No, it's not. You want it, you're gonna have to win it.

225
00:12:23,740 --> 00:12:27,030
So are we not having dinner at all?

226
00:12:27,200 --> 00:12:30,990
Come on, let's go. It's time to get serious. Huddle up.

227
00:12:31,450 --> 00:12:33,540
Keep your head in the game.

228
00:12:33,710 --> 00:12:37,040
It's hard, you know? His huddle's close to the Dutch girl.

229
00:12:38,420 --> 00:12:42,050
If I take Chandler out of the running, will you be able to focus?

230
00:12:42,210 --> 00:12:45,180
- What are you gonna do?     - Just make sure he catches the ball.

231
00:12:45,340 --> 00:12:46,340
I'll do the rest.

232
00:12:46,510 --> 00:12:49,430
- Come on, you wuss!     - Okay, come on.

233
00:12:50,260 --> 00:12:52,060
- Go, Cha... Chandler.     - I got it!

234
00:12:52,220 --> 00:12:54,350
Come on! This way! Come on!

235
00:12:54,770 --> 00:12:56,520
- Look out!     - Oof!

236
00:12:59,940 --> 00:13:03,030
Tackled by a girl! Bet you don't see that every day.

237
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:06,700
Whoa, whoa, whoa! What's with the tackling?

238
00:13:06,860 --> 00:13:08,700
What?

239
00:13:08,870 --> 00:13:10,580
I just touched him and he went over.

240
00:13:11,450 --> 00:13:14,750
Okay. You wanna play rough? We can play rough.

241
00:13:14,910 --> 00:13:17,870
Let's get ready to rumble!

242
00:13:57,750 --> 00:13:59,920
- Go, go, go!     - Get her! Get her!

243
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:05,630
I love this game!

244
00:14:08,680 --> 00:14:09,880
Where'd you get that?

245
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:12,600
I went really long.

246
00:14:13,970 --> 00:14:15,810
Forty-two to 21.

247
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:18,430
Like the turkey, Ross is done!

248
00:14:20,060 --> 00:14:23,270
You got to pick first, so you got the better team.

249
00:14:23,440 --> 00:14:26,440
Pathetic! Why can't you just accept that we're winning...

250
00:14:26,610 --> 00:14:27,940
...because I'm better than you?

251
00:14:28,110 --> 00:14:31,990
Oh, what a great argument. Exhaling!

252
00:14:32,740 --> 00:14:34,490
All right, I'll prove it to you. Okay?

253
00:14:34,660 --> 00:14:38,580
I'll trade you Joey for Rachel and I'll still win the game.

254
00:14:38,750 --> 00:14:41,120
What? The guys against the girls?

255
00:14:41,290 --> 00:14:44,840
That's ridiculous because I'm only down by three touchdowns.

256
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,750
Oh, then bring it on!

257
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:50,220
Unless you're afraid you might lose to a bunch of girls.

258
00:14:52,430 --> 00:14:55,810
Fine. Rachel, you're with Monica. Joey, you're with me.

259
00:14:56,100 --> 00:14:58,140
I can not believe you're trading me.

260
00:14:58,310 --> 00:15:01,480
Let's see what it's like to be on a winning team for a change.

261
00:15:01,650 --> 00:15:03,310
You're gonna let me play?

262
00:15:03,770 --> 00:15:05,270
All right, then!

263
00:15:06,110 --> 00:15:07,900
The game is over? We eat now?

264
00:15:08,070 --> 00:15:09,990
No, the game's not over. We're switching teams.

265
00:15:10,150 --> 00:15:14,530
Chandler finds me so intimidating that it's better if we're on the same team.

266
00:15:14,700 --> 00:15:16,780
Okay, let's play. Let's go.

267
00:15:16,950 --> 00:15:18,370
Oh, uh, hold on a second.

268
00:15:18,540 --> 00:15:21,080
Ahem. Where do Dutch people come from?

269
00:15:28,550 --> 00:15:30,510
Uh, well, the, uh...

270
00:15:30,670 --> 00:15:33,930
...Pennsylvania Dutch come from Pennsylvania.

271
00:15:34,470 --> 00:15:36,510
And the, uh, other Dutch people?

272
00:15:36,680 --> 00:15:39,470
They come from somewhere near the Netherlands, right?

273
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:41,520
Nice try.

274
00:15:41,690 --> 00:15:43,940
The Netherlands is this make-believe place...

275
00:15:44,100 --> 00:15:47,110
...where Peter Pan and Tinker Bell come from.

276
00:15:48,320 --> 00:15:49,860
Oh, my.

277
00:15:50,650 --> 00:15:53,700
Enough "geography for the insane." Let's play ball.

278
00:15:53,860 --> 00:15:56,240
No. No, I'm not playing with this guy.

279
00:15:56,410 --> 00:15:58,990
- Oh, fine with me.     - I've had enough of this.

280
00:15:59,160 --> 00:16:03,080
Let's just cut to the chase. Heidi, which of my boys do you like?

281
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:05,080
What are you doing?

282
00:16:05,250 --> 00:16:06,880
What are you doing?

283
00:16:08,590 --> 00:16:10,090
Which do I like?

284
00:16:10,260 --> 00:16:14,010
Yeah, for dating, general merriment, taking back to your windmill?

285
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:17,260
Well, if I had to choose right now...

286
00:16:17,430 --> 00:16:20,140
...which, by the way, I find really weird...

287
00:16:21,560 --> 00:16:23,640
...I would have to say Chandler.

288
00:16:24,060 --> 00:16:25,400
Yes!

289
00:16:26,190 --> 00:16:29,570
Wait a minute. She didn't understand the question.

290
00:16:29,730 --> 00:16:32,940
Why don't you have Captain Hook explain it to her?

291
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:36,360
I'm sorry. That is my truth.

292
00:16:36,530 --> 00:16:40,120
You hear that? That is her truth, Mr. "I'll Let You Have Her"!

293
00:16:40,290 --> 00:16:43,080
I win! You suck! I rule all!

294
00:16:43,250 --> 00:16:45,870
Mini-wave in celebration of me!

295
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:55,010
I am now thinking I would like to change my answer to "no one."

296
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:56,760
What?

297
00:16:57,340 --> 00:16:59,850
I now find you shallow, and, um...

298
00:17:00,010 --> 00:17:01,760
...a dork.

299
00:17:02,310 --> 00:17:03,850
Bye-bye.

300
00:17:04,350 --> 00:17:05,850
Heh. Nice going.

301
00:17:06,020 --> 00:17:08,690
You just saved yourself a couple months of sex.

302
00:17:09,570 --> 00:17:11,900
It doesn't matter, because she picked me.

303
00:17:12,070 --> 00:17:14,150
From now on, I get the dates...

304
00:17:14,320 --> 00:17:17,950
...and you stay home on Saturday nights watching Ready, Set, Cook!

305
00:17:18,490 --> 00:17:21,370
Save the breakthroughs for therapy. The clock is ticking.

306
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:24,250
We have no time, and we are losing to girls.

307
00:17:24,410 --> 00:17:26,040
We're not gonna lose to girls.

308
00:17:26,210 --> 00:17:27,790
It's 42-21!

309
00:17:27,960 --> 00:17:31,420
This sucks! I was just up by that much!

310
00:17:32,420 --> 00:17:35,920
Are we playing football or what? Come on, you hairy-backed Marys!

311
00:17:37,510 --> 00:17:40,850
We have to do this. We're playing for women everywhere.

312
00:17:41,010 --> 00:17:43,560
Think about every lousy date you ever had.

313
00:17:43,720 --> 00:17:46,770
Every guy who kept one eye on the TV while you were making out.

314
00:17:46,940 --> 00:17:50,190
Oh, my God. You dated someone with a glass eye too?

315
00:17:52,020 --> 00:17:55,990
Come on, okay? This is for all womankind. Let's kill them!

316
00:17:56,150 --> 00:17:57,860
Yeah! Kill them!

317
00:17:59,110 --> 00:18:01,410
All right, I want to kill them too.

318
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:03,240
But they're boys.

319
00:18:03,410 --> 00:18:06,370
You know, how are we gonna beat three boys?

320
00:18:35,860 --> 00:18:38,570
A minute and a half left, and we're down by two points.

321
00:18:38,740 --> 00:18:39,950
Two points, ladies.

322
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:48,370
Phoebe, you do a buttonhook again.

323
00:18:48,540 --> 00:18:49,910
Rachel, you go long.

324
00:18:50,080 --> 00:18:53,840
No, don't make me go long. Use me. They never cover me.

325
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:55,750
Honey, there's a reason.

326
00:18:57,090 --> 00:18:59,760
I'm not lame, okay? I can do something.

327
00:19:00,010 --> 00:19:02,510
Would you let me throw? This is my game too.

328
00:19:02,720 --> 00:19:04,390
Let her throw the ball.

329
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:08,270
Sweep behind, I'll pitch it. You throw it downfield to Phoebe.

330
00:19:08,430 --> 00:19:09,520
Thank you.

331
00:19:09,690 --> 00:19:11,060
- Break!     - Break!

332
00:19:11,230 --> 00:19:12,900
All right, here we go.

333
00:19:13,060 --> 00:19:15,360
Thirty-two, 71, hike!

334
00:19:15,520 --> 00:19:17,940
One Mississippi, two Mississippi, three Mississippi!

335
00:19:23,410 --> 00:19:24,990
Go, go, go!

336
00:19:25,740 --> 00:19:27,120
Catch it!

337
00:19:29,410 --> 00:19:32,420
- I'm so sorry. Are you okay?     - No, I'm not okay!

338
00:19:33,750 --> 00:19:36,210
They were coming at me, and I didn't know what to do.

339
00:19:36,380 --> 00:19:38,460
Thirty seconds left on the timer.

340
00:19:38,630 --> 00:19:41,760
So we get to take that, uh, stupid troll thing home.

341
00:19:41,930 --> 00:19:44,890
Come on! Hurry! We're running out of time.

342
00:19:45,050 --> 00:19:46,760
- Huddle up!     - Okay.

343
00:19:48,220 --> 00:19:51,100
Oh! This is our last huddle!

344
00:19:51,940 --> 00:19:54,940
All right, Phoebe, get open. Rachel...

345
00:19:55,110 --> 00:19:57,610
- ...go long.     - Okay.

346
00:19:57,770 --> 00:19:59,480
Break!

347
00:20:46,660 --> 00:20:49,410
Ahh! I did it! Touchdown! We did it!

348
00:20:53,120 --> 00:20:57,460
You know? Funny thing, actually. The end zone starts at that pole.

349
00:20:57,670 --> 00:20:59,670
So you're five feet short. So...

350
00:20:59,840 --> 00:21:02,550
...ha-ha-ha, we win!

351
00:21:03,840 --> 00:21:05,300
Yes, yes, yes!

352
00:21:05,470 --> 00:21:07,510
Wait, explain something, though.

353
00:21:07,680 --> 00:21:12,010
If nobody tagged Rachel, then isn't the play still going?

354
00:21:17,230 --> 00:21:19,730
- Let me in! Let me in!     - No way! Let go!

355
00:21:19,900 --> 00:21:22,860
Let go? I'm a tiny little woman!

356
00:21:23,320 --> 00:21:25,320
Guys, come on, it's Thanksgiving!

357
00:21:25,490 --> 00:21:27,860
It's not important who wins or loses.

358
00:21:28,030 --> 00:21:30,990
The important thing is the Dutch girl picked me!

359
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:37,160
Me, not you! Holland loves Chandler! Thank you, Amsterdam! Good night!

360
00:21:41,380 --> 00:21:42,710
Ow!

361
00:21:44,880 --> 00:21:46,970
We should play football more often.

362
00:21:47,130 --> 00:21:49,640
Maybe there's a league we could join.

363
00:21:49,890 --> 00:21:52,930
Isn't there a "national football league"?

364
00:21:53,850 --> 00:21:56,600
Yes, there is. They play on Sundays and Monday nights.

365
00:21:56,770 --> 00:21:59,400
Oh, shoot! I work Monday nights.

366
00:22:02,070 --> 00:22:05,940
This stuffing is amazing. Do you think we should bring them some?

367
00:22:06,110 --> 00:22:08,200
When they're hungry, they'll come in.

368
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:11,240
- Let go!     - No, you let go!

369
00:22:13,200 --> 00:22:16,250
How come it's always us left holding the ball?

370
00:22:16,410 --> 00:22:20,250
I don't know. I guess the other people just don't care enough.

371
00:22:25,920 --> 00:22:28,800
Hey, it's starting to snow.

372
00:22:33,060 --> 00:22:36,220
- Give it to me! Let go!     - Let it go! Come on, let go!

